# The archives under data/ are records, not source code.
#
# Git's default on Windows is core.autocrlf=true: every file it considers text
# is checked out with CRLF line endings. The release runner is a Windows
# machine, and that conversion cost real data — `readStations` split the last
# column of stations.csv without stripping the carriage return, so the column
# name came out as "elevation\r", every station's altitude was stored as null,
# and the 552 most recent nationwide days silently failed the "needs an
# altitude" filter. The shipped database went out missing a year and a half.
#
# The readers no longer care either way (they split on /\r?\n/), but these
# files should not be rewritten on their way out of the repository in the first
# place: they are byte-for-byte archives, their checksums should match across
# platforms, and nothing in them is edited by hand.
data/** -text

# Scripts that are executed rather than read. CRLF breaks a shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf
